{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_12","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"category\":1,\"caption_or_event\":\"Matthew Tokson, “What Is Fourth Amendment Law Going Forward?”\",\"court\":\"Major doctrinal commentary—Dorf on Law\",\"date\":\"2026-07-13\",\"cite_or_docket\":\"https://www.dorfonlaw.org/2026/07/what-is-fourth-amendment-law-going.html\",\"why_it_matters\":\"Tokson argues that Chatrie creates a new framework emphasizing revealing data, surveillance capacity, and meaningful waiver while substantially weakening duration and third-party-disclosure limits.\",\"discovery_path\":\"Fourth Amendment teaching instructor legal research commentary July 2026 doctrinal update\",\"confidence\":\"high\"}\n{\"category\":2,\"caption_or_event\":\"United States v. Holcomb (reissued divided-panel opinion)\",\"court\":\"U.S. Court of Appeals for the Ninth Circuit\",\"date\":\"2026-07-17\",\"cite_or_docket\":\"No. 23-469\",\"why_it_matters\":\"The panel held that probable cause must persist during warrant execution and that officers must stop searching when newly discovered exculpatory evidence completely dissipates it.\",\"discovery_path\":\"Ninth Circuit July 20 2026 CSAM valid warrant stop searching exculpatory evidence caption\",\"confidence\":\"high\"}\n{\"category\":3,\"caption_or_event\":\"United States v. Brillhart\",\"court\":\"U.S. Court of Appeals for the Eleventh Circuit\",\"date\":\"2026-07-09\",\"cite_or_docket\":\"No. 24-13226\",\"why_it_matters\":\"The Eleventh Circuit joined the Fifth and Sixth Circuits in treating Google’s human-seeded hash matching as a private search, deepening their split with the Second, Fourth, and Ninth Circuits.\",\"discovery_path\":\"reasonable expectation privacy curtilage open fields third party digital circuit July 2026 opinion\",\"confidence\":\"high\"}\n{\"category\":0,\"caption_or_event\":\"NO-NEW-DEVELOPMENTS\"}\n{\"category\":5,\"caption_or_event\":\"United States v. Holcomb (reissued divided-panel opinion)\",\"court\":\"U.S. Court of Appeals for the Ninth Circuit\",\"date\":\"2026-07-17\",\"cite_or_docket\":\"No. 23-469\",\"why_it_matters\":\"The panel invalidated an overbroad digital-warrant provision and held that officers unreasonably executed otherwise valid authority by continuing after probable cause dissipated.\",\"discovery_path\":\"Ninth Circuit July 20 2026 CSAM valid warrant stop searching exculpatory evidence caption\",\"confidence\":\"high\"}\n{\"category\":0,\"caption_or_event\":\"NO-NEW-DEVELOPMENTS\"}\n{\"category\":7,\"caption_or_event\":\"United States v. Holcomb (reissued divided-panel opinion)\",\"court\":\"U.S. Court of Appeals for the Ninth Circuit\",\"date\":\"2026-07-17\",\"cite_or_docket\":\"No. 23-469\",\"why_it_matters\":\"The panel ordered suppression, rejecting plain view and concluding that good faith ended when probable cause dissipated during the officers’ execution of the warrant.\",\"discovery_path\":\"Ninth Circuit July 20 2026 CSAM valid warrant stop searching exculpatory evidence caption\",\"confidence\":\"high\"}\n{\"category\":0,\"caption_or_event\":\"NO-NEW-DEVELOPMENTS\"}\n{\"category\":0,\"caption_or_event\":\"NO-NEW-DEVELOPMENTS\"}\n{\"category\":0,\"caption_or_event\":\"NO-NEW-DEVELOPMENTS\"}\n{\"category\":0,\"caption_or_event\":\"NO-NEW-DEVELOPMENTS\"}\n{\"category\":0,\"caption_or_event\":\"NO-NEW-DEVELOPMENTS\"}\n{\"category\":0,\"caption_or_event\":\"NO-NEW-DEVELOPMENTS\"}"}}
